    "body": "<!-- myque:id=01a08ff0-0bae-741e-9318-331fdafe0b96 -->\n<!-- myque:projection=github/v1 -->\nManaged by myque. Title, body, myque:* labels and work state are projected; use comments for discussion.\n\n**Myque:** IO11 — <code>01a08ff0-0bae-741e-9318-331fdafe0b96</code>\n**Kind:** milestone · **State:** active · **Ready:** no\n**Tags:** <code>github</code>, <code>io</code>\n**Canonical:** [\\.tasks/items/01a08ff0\\-0bae\\-741e\\-9318\\-331fdafe0b96\\.md](https://github.com/iceice666/slime_os/blob/main/.tasks/items/01a08ff0-0bae-741e-9318-331fdafe0b96.md)\n\n## Relationships\n- Parent: IO10 — open — [#39](https://github.com/iceice666/slime_os/issues/39)\n- Dependencies:\n  - IO4 — done — [\\.tasks/items/01a04919\\-7400\\-75da\\-bdab\\-760af8f246f1\\.md](https://github.com/iceice666/slime_os/blob/main/.tasks/items/01a04919-7400-75da-bdab-760af8f246f1.md)\n  - IO3 — done — [\\.tasks/items/01a04919\\-7400\\-778b\\-93f0\\-8e99df9aeb79\\.md](https://github.com/iceice666/slime_os/blob/main/.tasks/items/01a04919-7400-778b-93f0-8e99df9aeb79.md)\n\n## Implementation\n- [#32](https://github.com/iceice666/slime_os/pull/32) — IO11: a TCP client byte stream over virtio\\-net, echoed byte for byte under QEMU — open · ready · CI passing · review none\n  - Head: <code>CG-AA/slime_os:feat/network-tcp-client</code> at <code>12ba5eac2db5484b345f59ecfd56cdc183da89a9</code>; base: <code>iceice666/slime_os:main</code>\n\nCI/review facts are GitHub observations for the displayed head; they are not myque completion evidence.\n\n---\n\n# QEMU TCP client byte stream over virtio-net: ARP, IPv4, ICMP echo reply, TCP open/send/recv/close to one declared destination\n\n## Context\n\nA new composition, `sel4-io-tcp`, binds `network-service` to `virtio-net-driver` over the\nIO0 rings and loans the IO3 probe already uses, and runs smoltcp inside the service: ARP,\nIPv4, ICMP echo reply, and a TCP client to one exact generation-declared destination. The\nservice's own address and MAC are generation data (`contracts/network-interface/v1`), its\ntick rate comes from the root's clock authority (`CLOCK_RATE_READ`), and client bytes travel\nin an IO0 queue per client with the existing 56-byte request and 24-byte completion as\npayloads. The QEMU peer is a frame-level Python responder on the same UDP socket backend the\nlink plane uses, so every frame is observed and nothing depends on host networking.\n\nNo UDP, DNS, listen/accept, IPv6, or DHCP. Backend independence is not claimed: one backend\nis exercised.\n\n## Exit conditions\n\nUnder QEMU, `just io_tcp_check` observes: the service reports its declared interface and a\nlink that is up, answers the peer's ARP request and ICMP echo requests, opens a TCP\nconnection to the declared destination, sends 4096 bytes and receives them back byte for\nbyte, closes it, is refused by the peer on a second declared port, refuses an undeclared\ndestination before any frame leaves, and the plane ends healthy; `just io_link_check`\nstays green; the intruder's refusals hold with zero frames at the peer.\n\n## Verification\n\nGates: `just io_tcp_check`, `just io_network_check`, `just io_link_check`,\n`just link_peer_check`, `just sel4_gate_control_check`, `just contracts_check`,\n`just test_host`, `just test_sel4_root`\n",
